      "answer": "To save a checklist array to `localStorage`, first convert the array to a JSON string using `JSON.stringify()`. Then, use `localStorage.setItem(key, jsonString)` to store it. For example, `localStorage.setItem('checklist', JSON.stringify(myArray))`. To restore it, retrieve the string using `localStorage.getItem('checklist')` and parse it back into an array using `JSON.parse()`. Finally, you can use `JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('checklist'))` to get the original array. \n\nSources: \n1. MDN Web Docs: Window: localStorage property (for general localStorage usage).\n2. MDN Web Docs: Storage: setItem() method (for the setItem function).\n\nSources read:\n- https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/localStorage\n- https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Storage/setItem"
